{"nodes": [{"id": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_week_01_lead_triage", "label": "Week 01: inbound lead triage and routing", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L1-L20", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_six_step_triage_workflow", "label": "Six-step inbound lead triage workflow", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L3-L15", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Steps 1-4 (disqualify, icp_fit, segment, intent) are judgments and go to a model; step 5 (routing) is a rule and runs in code for every runner; step 6 (writing the email) is prose and goes to Claude because Jev structurally cannot produce it. Splitting the workflow this way is what makes the cost comparison meaningful."}, {"id": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_step_6_email_writing", "label": "Step 6: write the first-touch email", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L137-L184", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "29 of 60 leads earned an email at a mean of 4,052 ms and $0.0026 each; the other 31 were rejected or nurtured and cost nothing to write to. The architecture is not 'Jev instead of Claude' but Jev deciding which leads are worth paying Claude for."}, {"id": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_thinking_disabled_correction", "label": "Fairness correction: extended thinking disabled", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L59-L63", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Claude CLI enables extended thinking by default; Haiku spent ~1,800 thinking tokens and 22 seconds per lead deciding whether a resume was a resume. MAX_THINKING_TOKENS=0 took the same call to 2.6 seconds. Nobody would ship lead triage with thinking on, so benchmarking it that way would have been dishonest by a factor of 23."}, {"id": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_prompt_cache_pricing_correction", "label": "Fairness correction: prompt-cache-aware pricing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L65-L68", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sonnet's CLI caches the system prompt so its real tokens land in cache_creation and cache_read, not input_tokens. Cache reads were being charged at full input price; writes bill at 1.25x and reads at 0.1x, and Claude gets credit for that saving because a production deployment would get it too."}, {"id": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_cli_overhead_calibration_correction", "label": "Fairness correction: CLI token-overhead calibration", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L70-L74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Because of prompt caching, the calibration probe read the wrong field and measured Sonnet's CLI scaffolding as 2 tokens instead of 2,214, so Claude was billed for a prompt it did not write. Summing all three token buckets fixed it and dropped Sonnet's cost per thousand from $7.71 to $3.01."}, {"id": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_split_call_ablation", "label": "Split-call ablation (one Claude call per question)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L80-L99", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Run to answer the 'you strawmanned Claude by asking four questions at once' objection. It helped: icp_fit 51.7% to 71.7%, route accuracy 53.3% to 61.7%, Brier nearly halved. It also cost 5.2x the latency and 2.9x the money and still lost to Jev by 28 points."}, {"id": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_intent_optimism_bias", "label": "Jev's half-level intent optimism bias", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L103-L108", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Intent is Jev's worst number at 75% against Sonnet's 82%. Of 15 errors, 14 are off by exactly one level and every one runs the same direction: it reads leads as keener than they are. A systematic bias of about half a level is fixable with a threshold rather than a different model."}, {"id": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_competitor_blind_spot", "label": "Jev's competitor blind spot (L009 Clay, L010 Apollo.io)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L110-L135", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Jev's two disqualify misses were a RevOps manager at Clay and a PM at Apollo.io, waved through at 0.06 and 0.18. Naming the competitor set in round 2 flipped both for Sonnet (0.95 and 0.97) but never moved Jev over the line: Jev is better at applying a rubric you describe, Claude is better at using a fact you just told it. The real fix is a domain blocklist in code, not a model."}, {"id": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_recommended_architecture", "label": "Recommended production architecture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L186-L212", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Domain blocklist first because it is the one step with a right answer needing no model; Jev for the four fuzzy judgments; routing in code because it is five branches that are free, instant, untestable-by-drift and unit testable; Sonnet only on qualified leads. Jev's Brier of 0.041 against Sonnet's 0.130 means the probability is usable for an auto-approve band above 0.9 and a human-review band at 0.4-0.6. Send intent to human review until recalibrated."}, {"id": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_end_to_end_cost_model", "label": "End-to-end cost per 1,000 inbound leads", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L167-L174", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Jev triage plus Sonnet writing costs $1.31 per 1,000 versus $4.28 for Sonnet doing both, 3.3x cheaper end to end, and the saving grows the worse your inbound is because junk never reaches the expensive step."}, {"id": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_partial_run_warning", "label": "Do not read the partial run", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L97-L99", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At 18 leads the split run showed 88.9% route accuracy and looked like it had closed the gap; at 60 leads it was 61.7%."}, {"id": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_cli_signature_leak", "label": "CLI environment leak in generated emails", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L175-L180", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "10 of 29 emails contain an em dash the prompt forbade, and the emails are signed with a name never supplied in the prompt, implying the CLI leaks something from the environment. Neither affects triage numbers since no judgment depends on a signature."}], "edges": [{"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_week_01_lead_triage", "target": "week_01_lead_triage_rubric_rubric", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L18", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_week_01_lead_triage", "target": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_six_step_triage_workflow", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L3-L15", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_week_01_lead_triage", "target": "src_spec_questions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L76", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_six_step_triage_workflow", "target": "src_spec_disqualify_question", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L5-L6", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_six_step_triage_workflow", "target": "src_spec_icp_fit_question", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L7", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_six_step_triage_workflow", "target": "src_spec_segment_question", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L8", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_six_step_triage_workflow", "target": "src_spec_intent_question", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_six_step_triage_workflow", "target": "src_spec_route", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L10", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_six_step_triage_workflow", "target": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_step_6_email_writing", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L11", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_step_6_email_writing", "target": "src_step6_email_main", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L143", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_step_6_email_writing", "target": "src_step6_email_jev_has_no_text_primitive", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L139-L146", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_thinking_disabled_correction", "target": "src_claude_runner__invoke", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L59-L63", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_prompt_cache_pricing_correction", "target": "src_claude_runner_input_cost", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L65-L68", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_prompt_cache_pricing_correction", "target": "src_claude_runner_pricing", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L65-L68", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_cli_overhead_calibration_correction", "target": "src_claude_runner_calibrate", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L70-L74", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_cli_overhead_calibration_correction", "target": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_prompt_cache_pricing_correction", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L70-L72", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_split_call_ablation", "target": "src_split_runner_claudesplitrunner", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L89", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_partial_run_warning", "target": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_split_call_ablation", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L97-L99", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_intent_optimism_bias", "target": "src_spec_intent_question", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L103-L108", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_intent_optimism_bias", "target": "src_jev_runner__intent_label", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L103-L108", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_competitor_blind_spot", "target": "src_spec_competitor_clarification", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L115-L118", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_competitor_blind_spot", "target": "src_score_competitors_leaked", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L110-L113", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_recommended_architecture", "target": "src_spec_route", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L199-L203", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_recommended_architecture", "target": "src_score_brier", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L205-L209", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_recommended_architecture", "target": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_intent_optimism_bias", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L211-L212", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_end_to_end_cost_model", "target": "src_step6_email_qualified_only_gating", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L167-L174", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_cli_signature_leak", "target": "src_step6_email_system", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L175-L180", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_intent_optimism_bias", "target": "src_split_runner_error_correlation_hypothesis", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L103-L108", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_end_to_end_cost_model", "target": "results_results", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L167-L174", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_cli_signature_leak", "target": "week_01_lead_triage_readme_step_6_email_writing", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md", "source_location": "L175-L180", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "benchmark_fairness_corrections", "label": "Benchmark fairness corrections applied before publishing", "nodes": ["week_01_lead_triage_readme_thinking_disabled_correction", "week_01_lead_triage_readme_prompt_cache_pricing_correction", "week_01_lead_triage_readme_cli_overhead_calibration_correction", "readme_fix_the_unfair_thing", "readme_measure_the_network"], "relation": "form", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md"}, {"id": "benchmark_run_pipeline", "label": "Benchmark run pipeline: build, run, ablate, write, score", "nodes": ["src_build_dataset_main", "src_bench_main", "src_split_runner_main", "src_step6_email_main", "src_score_main", "results_results"], "relation": "participate_in", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "week-01-lead-triage/README.md"}]}